"""Battles of Wales (battles.html): every recorded battle we can place, from the Romans to the Falklands, and who it was against.

Each battle is B(id, English name, Welsh name, year, date EN, date CY, (lat, lon) or None, era, side EN, side CY, story EN, story CY, see, win).
`geo` None means the place is not known for sure: the battle is listed but left off the map. Battles outside Wales still go
on the map if they fall inside its frame (Chester, Hereford); others (Bosworth, Mametz Wood) are listed with `away` in the date.
`win` is "w" for a Welsh victory, "l" for a defeat, "o" for other (risings, battles where Welsh fought on both sides).
`VS` (at the bottom) says who each battle was against, from the keys in `AGAINST`; every battle must have one.
Tell every battle with pride in the people who fought it (EDITORIAL.md). A defeat is told as a stand, never as a failure.
"""


def B(id, en, cy, year, dEn, dCy, geo, era, sEn, sCy, tEn, tCy, see=(), win="w"):
    return dict(id=id, en=en, cy=cy, year=year, dEn=dEn, dCy=dCy, geo=geo, era=era, sEn=sEn, sCy=sCy, tEn=tEn, tCy=tCy, see=list(see), win=win)


